#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""ctlhq-install: link this repository's skills, agents and rules file into the host folders of a home.

Usage:
  ctlhq-install [--dry-run] [--replace] [--agents-md] [--home DIR]   create or repair every link
  ctlhq-install --check [--home DIR]                                 report drift, change nothing
  ctlhq-install --uninstall [--dry-run] [--home DIR]                 remove only what it installed

--home defaults to $HOME. Links are absolute paths to each layer's resolved location.

Layers:
  A layer is a folder holding skills/, agents/ or home/, and optionally docs/install.tsv.
  The installer reads the ordered list of layers from <home>/.ctlhq/layers.toml, never
  from any other home. With no file, the only layer is this repository: the parent of
  this tool's bin/ folder, found from the tool's real path, so a renamed or moved folder
  works when the installer runs again. Skills and agents from every layer are linked
  side by side. The same skill or agent name in two layers is refused (exit 1, nothing
  changed). A listed layer that is not a folder holding skills/, agents/ or home/ is a
  usage error (exit 2, nothing changed), in every mode.

<home>/.ctlhq/layers.toml, every key optional:
  layers = ["~/code/public-skills", "~/code/my-skills"]
                       ordered layer folders; absolute or ~/ paths, where ~ is the home
                       given with --home. Default: this repository alone.
  agents_md = true     write <home>/.codex/AGENTS.md (see Rules file). Default false.
  not_shipped = ["vendor-skill"]
                       skill names that no mode links, checks or removes, for example
                       a skill another tool's installer owns.
  [hosts]
  why = ["claude", "codex"]
                       per-machine host rows. Each overrides the layers' host tables for
                       one skill that a layer ships.

What it links:
  skills/<name>/SKILL.md   <home>/.claude/skills/<name> and <home>/.codex/skills/<name>
                           (default hosts claude,codex). A layer's docs/install.tsv
                           (skill<TAB>hosts, hosts from claude, codex, agents) overrides one
                           of that layer's skills; "agents" is <home>/.agents/skills/.
  agents/<file>.md         <home>/.claude/agents/<file>.md

Rules file (only with agents_md = true, or --agents-md, which saves that line in
layers.toml once the file below is written or already correct; while a file of the
user's own stays in place, --agents-md saves nothing):
  <home>/.codex/AGENTS.md is a generated file: a first-line marker naming its sources,
  then each layer's home/AGENTS.md joined in layer order. <home>/.claude/CLAUDE.md is
  never touched; it may include ~/.codex/AGENTS.md with one @ line.
  A link at that path is removed first, so nothing is ever written through it.
  A real file without the marker is a "copy": left in place, exit 1, unless --replace
  moves it to <home>/.ctlhq-backups/ first.
  Another tool may own a block in the file, marked <!-- <tool>:<id> --> ... <!-- /<tool>:<id> -->
  (a tool's own installer adds it). Such a block that differs from the layers is "managed"
  drift, named with the tool: copy the new block into a layer's home/AGENTS.md. Install
  never overwrites it (exit 1).
  Any other difference is "stale" drift, and install rewrites the file.
  With agents_md off (false or no line), a generated file there is "unwanted": install
  moves it to <home>/.ctlhq-backups/ and prints the @ line the user may remove from
  ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md. A file without the marker is never touched.

Install rules:
  A missing link is created (parent folders too). A link to the right place is left alone.
  A link pointing elsewhere is repointed and reported. A real file or folder is never
  deleted: it is reported "copy in place, not replaced" and the run exits 1, unless
  --replace is given, which first moves it to <home>/.ctlhq-backups/<YYYY-MM-DD>/<same
  relative path>. A link into a layer in a host folder the skill is not listed for (for
  example .codex/skills/<name> for a claude,agents skill) is removed and reported.
  A link in a host folder, under a name no layer ships, is the installer's own leftover
  (an old skill or agent name after a rename) only when all four hold: the link's text is
  an absolute path; that path names an item directly inside <layer>/skills or
  <layer>/agents of a listed layer; that skills or agents folder exists; and the item
  itself is gone. Install removes such a "stale" link and prints one "remove stale" line
  each. Every other link is never touched: a relative link, a link deeper inside a layer,
  a link into a layer whose skills or agents folder is missing, a link outside every
  layer, and a link whose target exists.
  Apart from stale links, names no layer ships are never touched; not_shipped names,
  synced/ and .system/ are never touched at all.
  The PATH line for bin/ and the Stop hook line are printed for the operator to apply;
  the installer never edits shell files or settings.json.

--check prints one line per layer (path, skill, agent and link counts), then each drift
on one line: missing (no link), copy (a real file or folder), broken (a link into a
missing folder), elsewhere (a link outside every layer), wrong (a link to another item in
a layer), extra (a link into a layer in a host folder the skill is not listed for), stale
(the installer's own leftover, as defined under Install rules; a "fix:" line follows).
For the rules file it also reports link (a link where the generated file belongs), stale
and managed, or, with agents_md off, unwanted (a generated file still in place).
Exit 1 on any drift, 0 when clean.
--dry-run prints every action, including unchanged links, and changes nothing; its exit
code is the one the real run would return.
--uninstall removes the links for every skill and agent the layers ship that point into
a layer, in every host folder, and a <home>/.codex/AGENTS.md whose first line is the
marker, after a backup. It also removes each stale link (as defined under Install
rules). It lists, and leaves, every other link in a host folder, under a name no layer
ships, that points into a layer, apart from not_shipped names, synced/ and .system/. It
then prints the @ line the user may remove from ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md, and, when
layers.toml holds agents_md = true, that the line stays there, so a later install writes
the rules file again.

Operator rule encoded: "Any change that widens a sandbox, writable root, network rule,
permission, hook, or global instruction file needs the operator's yes first."

Exit 0 success or clean, 1 drift, a copy or managed block left in place, or a refused
duplicate name, 2 usage error.
"""
from __future__ import annotations

import datetime
import json
import os
import re
import shutil
import sys
from pathlib import Path
from typing import NamedTuple, Optional

ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent
HOST_DIRS = {
    "claude": ".claude/skills",
    "codex": ".codex/skills",
    "agents": ".agents/skills",
}
DEFAULT_HOSTS = ("claude", "codex")
AGENTS_DIR = ".claude/agents"
LAYER_PARTS = ("skills", "agents", "home")
NEVER_TOUCH = {"synced", ".system"}
SETTINGS = ".ctlhq/layers.toml"
RULES = ".codex/AGENTS.md"
MARKER = "<!-- generated by ctlhq-install from "
CLAUDE_INCLUDE = "@~/.codex/AGENTS.md"
MANAGED_BLOCK = re.compile(r"^<!-- (([A-Za-z0-9_.-]+):[^\s>]+) -->$.*?^<!-- /\1 -->$", re.M | re.S)
LINK_KINDS = ("ok", "missing", "copy", "broken", "elsewhere", "wrong", "extra", "stale")
RULES_KINDS = ("link", "managed")


class Settings(NamedTuple):
    layers: tuple
    agents_md: bool
    not_shipped: frozenset
    hosts: dict


class Link(NamedTuple):
    path: Path
    source: Path
    wanted: bool  # False: a host folder the skill is not listed for; a link into a layer there is 'extra'
    layer: Path


class Rules(NamedTuple):
    path: Path
    text: str
    sources: tuple


class Duplicates(Exception):
    pass


def usage_error(msg: str) -> int:
    print(f"ctlhq-install: {msg}", file=sys.stderr)
    print("usage: ctlhq-install [--dry-run] [--check] [--uninstall] [--replace] [--agents-md] [--home DIR]",
          file=sys.stderr)
    return 2


def drop_comment(line: str) -> str:
    quote, i = None, 0
    while i < len(line):
        c = line[i]
        if quote:
            if c == "\\" and quote == '"':
                i += 1
            elif c == quote:
                quote = None
        elif c in "\"'":
            quote = c
        elif c == "#":
            return line[:i]
        i += 1
    return line


class Unterminated(ValueError):
    pass


def parse_value(s: str, where: str):
    """One TOML value: true, false, a quoted string, or a list of quoted strings. Returns (value, rest)."""
    s = s.lstrip()
    for word, value in (("true", True), ("false", False)):
        if s.startswith(word) and not s[len(word):len(word) + 1].isalnum():
            return value, s[len(word):]
    if s[:1] in ('"', "'"):
        q, out, i = s[0], [], 1
        while i < len(s):
            c = s[i]
            if q == '"' and c == "\\" and i + 1 < len(s):
                out.append(s[i + 1])
                i += 2
                continue
            if c == q:
                return "".join(out), s[i + 1:]
            out.append(c)
            i += 1
        raise ValueError(f"{where}: unterminated string")
    if s[:1] == "[":
        rest, items = s[1:], []
        while True:
            rest = rest.lstrip()
            if not rest:
                raise Unterminated(f"{where}: unterminated list")
            if rest[0] == "]":
                return items, rest[1:]
            if rest[0] not in ('"', "'"):
                raise ValueError(f"{where}: list items must be quoted strings")
            item, rest = parse_value(rest, where)
            items.append(item)
            rest = rest.lstrip()
            if rest[:1] == ",":
                rest = rest[1:]
            elif rest and rest[0] != "]":
                raise ValueError(f"{where}: expected , or ] in the list")
    raise ValueError(f"{where}: a value must be true, false, a quoted string or a list of quoted strings")


def parse_settings(text: str, name: str) -> dict:
    """The layers.toml subset: top-level keys, then an optional [hosts] table of skill = [hosts]."""
    top, hosts, table = {}, {}, None
    lines = text.split("\n")
    i = 0
    while i < len(lines):
        n, s = i + 1, drop_comment(lines[i]).strip()
        i += 1
        where = f"{name} line {n}"
        if not s:
            continue
        if s.startswith("[") and s.endswith("]") and "=" not in s:
            table = s[1:-1].strip()
            if table != "hosts":
                raise ValueError(f"{where}: unknown table [{table}]; the only table is [hosts]")
            continue
        key, eq, rest = s.partition("=")
        key = key.strip()
        if not eq or not re.fullmatch(r"[A-Za-z0-9_-]+", key):
            raise ValueError(f"{where}: expected key = value")
        while True:
            try:
                value, tail = parse_value(rest, where)
                break
            except Unterminated:
                if i >= len(lines):
                    raise
                rest += " " + drop_comment(lines[i]).strip()
                i += 1
        if tail.strip():
            raise ValueError(f"{where}: unexpected text after the value: {tail.strip()!r}")
        if key in (hosts if table == "hosts" else top):
            raise ValueError(f"{where}: {key} is set twice")
        if table == "hosts":
            if not isinstance(value, list) or not value or any(h not in HOST_DIRS for h in value):
                raise ValueError(f"{where}: {key} needs a list of hosts from {', '.join(HOST_DIRS)}")
            hosts[key] = tuple(value)
            continue
        kind = {"layers": list, "agents_md": bool, "not_shipped": list}.get(key)
        if kind is None:
            raise ValueError(f"{where}: unknown key {key}; keys are layers, agents_md, not_shipped and [hosts]")
        if not isinstance(value, kind):
            raise ValueError(f"{where}: {key} must be {'true or false' if kind is bool else 'a list of quoted strings'}")
        top[key] = value
    top["hosts"] = hosts
    return top


def layer_path(raw: str, home: Path, where: str) -> Path:
    if raw == "~" or raw.startswith("~/"):
        path = home / raw[2:]
    elif os.path.isabs(raw):
        path = Path(raw)
    else:
        raise ValueError(f"{where}: layer {raw!r} must be an absolute path or start with ~/")
    if not path.is_dir() or not any((path / part).is_dir() for part in LAYER_PARTS):
        raise ValueError(f"{where}: layer {raw} is not a folder holding skills/, agents/ or home/")
    return Path(os.path.realpath(path))


def load_settings(home: Path) -> Settings:
    path = home / SETTINGS
    raw = {"hosts": {}}
    if os.path.lexists(path):
        if not path.is_file():
            raise ValueError(f"{path} is not a file")
        raw = parse_settings(path.read_text(encoding="utf-8"), str(path))
    layers = tuple(layer_path(p, home, str(path)) for p in raw.get("layers", [str(ROOT)]))
    if not layers:
        raise ValueError(f"{path}: layers is empty")
    if len(set(layers)) != len(layers):
        raise ValueError(f"{path}: a layer is listed twice")
    return Settings(layers, raw.get("agents_md", False), frozenset(raw.get("not_shipped", [])), raw["hosts"])


def save_agents_md(home: Path) -> None:
    """Set agents_md = true in layers.toml, keeping every other line."""
    path = home / SETTINGS
    lines = path.read_text(encoding="utf-8").split("\n") if path.is_file() else []
    first_table = next((i for i, line in enumerate(lines) if drop_comment(line).strip().startswith("[")), len(lines))
    found = next((i for i in range(first_table) if re.match(r"agents_md\s*=", drop_comment(lines[i]).strip())), None)
    if found is None:
        lines.insert(first_table, "agents_md = true")
    else:
        lines[found] = "agents_md = true"
    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    tmp = path.with_name(path.name + ".ctlhq-tmp")
    if os.path.lexists(tmp):
        tmp.unlink()
    with open(tmp, "x", encoding="utf-8") as f:  # "x" never follows a link
        f.write("\n".join(lines).rstrip("\n") + "\n")
    os.replace(tmp, path)


def read_hosts(layer: Path) -> dict:
    """skill -> tuple of hosts, from the layer's docs/install.tsv; raises ValueError on a bad row."""
    path = layer / "docs" / "install.tsv"
    out: dict = {}
    if not path.exists():
        return out
    for n, line in enumerate(path.read_text(encoding="utf-8").splitlines(), 1):
        if not line.strip() or line.startswith("#"):
            continue
        cells = line.split("\t")
        if n == 1 and cells[0] == "skill":
            continue
        if len(cells) != 2:
            raise ValueError(f"{path} line {n}: expected skill<TAB>hosts")
        hosts = tuple(h.strip() for h in cells[1].split(",") if h.strip())
        bad = [h for h in hosts if h not in HOST_DIRS]
        if bad or not hosts:
            raise ValueError(f"{path} line {n}: unknown host {','.join(bad) or '(none)'}")
        out[cells[0].strip()] = hosts
    return out


def joined_rules(home: Path, layers: tuple) -> Rules:
    sources = tuple(layer / "home" / "AGENTS.md" for layer in layers if (layer / "home" / "AGENTS.md").is_file())
    if not sources:
        raise ValueError("agents_md = true, but no layer holds home/AGENTS.md")
    parts = [p.read_text(encoding="utf-8") for p in sources]
    body = "\n".join(t if t.endswith("\n") else t + "\n" for t in parts)
    marker = f"{MARKER}{', '.join(map(str, sources))}. Edit those files and run ctlhq-install; edits here are overwritten. -->"
    return Rules(home / RULES, f"{marker}\n\n{body}", sources)


def build_plan(home: Path, settings: Settings):
    """Every Link the layers ship, and the Rules file when agents_md is on."""
    links, owner, dups = [], {}, []
    for layer in settings.layers:
        hosts_for = read_hosts(layer)
        found = [("skill", p.parent.name, p.parent) for p in sorted(layer.glob("skills/*/SKILL.md"))]
        found += [("agent", p.name, p) for p in sorted(layer.glob("agents/*.md"))]
        for kind, name, source in found:
            if kind == "skill" and name in NEVER_TOUCH:
                print(f"note: {layer}/skills/{name} uses a reserved name; skipped", file=sys.stderr)
                continue
            if kind == "skill" and name in settings.not_shipped:
                continue
            if (kind, name) in owner:
                dups.append(f"duplicate  {kind} {name} in {owner[kind, name]} and {layer}")
                continue
            owner[kind, name] = layer
            if kind == "agent":
                links.append(Link(home / AGENTS_DIR / name, source, True, layer))
                continue
            hosts = settings.hosts.get(name) or hosts_for.get(name, DEFAULT_HOSTS)
            for host, sub in HOST_DIRS.items():
                links.append(Link(home / sub / name, source, host in hosts, layer))
    if dups:
        raise Duplicates("\n".join(dups))
    unknown = sorted(set(settings.hosts) - {name for kind, name in owner if kind == "skill"})
    if unknown:
        raise ValueError(f"{home / SETTINGS}: [hosts] names a skill no layer ships: {', '.join(unknown)}")
    rules = joined_rules(home, settings.layers) if settings.agents_md else None
    return links, rules


def link_target(link: Path) -> Path:
    raw = Path(os.readlink(link))
    return raw if raw.is_absolute() else link.parent / raw


def inside_layers(p: Path, layers: tuple) -> bool:
    for candidate in (Path(os.path.realpath(p)), Path(os.path.normpath(p))):  # normpath: the item may be gone
        if any(candidate == layer or layer in candidate.parents for layer in layers):
            return True
    return False


def state(link: Path, source: Path, layers: tuple) -> str:
    """ok, missing, copy, broken, elsewhere, wrong."""
    if not os.path.lexists(link):
        return "missing"
    if not link.is_symlink():
        return "copy"
    target = link_target(link)
    if os.path.realpath(target) == str(source):
        return "ok"
    if not os.path.exists(target):
        return "broken"
    return "wrong" if inside_layers(target, layers) else "elsewhere"


def leftover(link: Path, layers: tuple) -> bool:
    """The installer's own leftover, such as an old skill name after a rename: the link text is absolute,
    names an item directly in an existing <layer>/skills or <layer>/agents folder, and that item is gone.
    Any other link may be the user's own, so it is never removed."""
    raw = Path(os.readlink(link))
    folders = {layer / part for layer in layers for part in ("skills", "agents")}
    return raw.is_absolute() and raw.parent in folders and raw.parent.is_dir() and not os.path.lexists(raw)


def unshipped_links(home: Path, settings: Settings, links: list) -> list:
    """(path, stale) for each link in a host folder, under a name no layer ships, that points into a layer.
    stale: the link is the installer's own leftover (see leftover)."""
    shipped = {link.path for link in links}
    skip = NEVER_TOUCH | settings.not_shipped
    out = []
    for folder in sorted({home / sub for sub in HOST_DIRS.values()} | {home / AGENTS_DIR}):
        for path in sorted(folder.iterdir()) if folder.is_dir() else ():
            if path in shipped or path.name in skip or not path.is_symlink():
                continue
            if inside_layers(link_target(path), settings.layers):
                out.append((path, leftover(path, settings.layers)))
    return out


def is_generated(path: Path) -> bool:
    if path.is_symlink() or not path.is_file():
        return False
    with open(path, encoding="utf-8", errors="replace") as f:
        return f.readline().startswith(MARKER)


def unwanted_rules(home: Path, rules: Optional[Rules]) -> bool:
    """A generated rules file in place while agents_md is off."""
    return rules is None and is_generated(home / RULES)


def print_include_note() -> None:
    print("~/.claude/CLAUDE.md may include the removed file. If it holds this line, you may delete it:")
    print(f"  {CLAUDE_INCLUDE}")


def rules_state(rules: Rules) -> str:
    """ok, missing, link, copy, managed, stale."""
    path = rules.path
    if not os.path.lexists(path):
        return "missing"
    if path.is_symlink():
        return "link"
    if not is_generated(path):
        return "copy"
    have = path.read_text(encoding="utf-8", errors="replace")
    if have == rules.text:
        return "ok"
    return "managed" if managed_drift(have, rules.text) else "stale"


def managed_drift(have: str, want: str) -> list:
    """The tools whose managed blocks differ between the file and the layers, in name order."""
    def blocks(text: str) -> dict:
        out = {}
        for m in MANAGED_BLOCK.finditer(text):
            out.setdefault(m.group(2), []).append(m.group(0))
        return out
    a, b = blocks(have), blocks(want)
    return sorted(t for t in a.keys() | b.keys() if a.get(t) != b.get(t))


def managed_tools(rules: Rules) -> str:
    return ", ".join(managed_drift(rules.path.read_text(encoding="utf-8", errors="replace"), rules.text))


def write_rules(rules: Rules) -> None:
    rules.path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    tmp = rules.path.with_name(rules.path.name + ".ctlhq-tmp")
    if os.path.lexists(tmp):
        tmp.unlink()
    with open(tmp, "x", encoding="utf-8") as f:  # "x" never follows a link
        f.write(rules.text)
    os.replace(tmp, rules.path)


def backup_path(home: Path, link: Path) -> Path:
    base = home / ".ctlhq-backups" / datetime.date.today().isoformat() / link.relative_to(home)
    dest, n = base, 1
    while os.path.lexists(dest):
        dest = base.with_name(f"{base.name}.{n}")
        n += 1
    return dest


def back_up(home: Path, path: Path, pre: str, dry: bool) -> None:
    dest = backup_path(home, path)
    print(f"{pre}back up    {show(path, home)} -> {show(dest, home)}")
    if not dry:
        dest.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        shutil.move(str(path), str(dest))


def show(link: Path, home: Path) -> str:
    return "~/" + str(link.relative_to(home))


def layer_count(settings: Settings) -> str:
    n = len(settings.layers)
    return f"{n} layer{'' if n == 1 else 's'}"


def summary(counts: dict, kinds: tuple) -> str:
    return ", ".join(f"{counts[k]} {k}" for k in kinds)


def do_check(home: Path, settings: Settings, links: list, rules: Optional[Rules]) -> int:
    layers = settings.layers
    unwanted = unwanted_rules(home, rules)
    kinds = LINK_KINDS + (RULES_KINDS if rules else ("unwanted",) if unwanted else ())
    counts = {k: 0 for k in kinds}
    lines = []
    per_layer = {layer: {"skills": set(), "agents": 0, "links": 0, "ok": 0} for layer in layers}
    for link, source, wanted, layer in links:
        tally = per_layer[layer]
        if source.is_dir():
            tally["skills"].add(source.name)
        else:
            tally["agents"] += 1
        if not wanted:
            if link.is_symlink() and inside_layers(link_target(link), layers):
                counts["extra"] += 1
                lines.append(f"extra      {show(link, home)} links into a layer; host not listed")
            continue
        tally["links"] += 1
        st = state(link, source, layers)
        counts[st] += 1
        if st == "ok":
            tally["ok"] += 1
        elif st == "missing":
            lines.append(f"missing    {show(link, home)}")
        elif st == "copy":
            lines.append(f"copy       {show(link, home)} is a real {'folder' if link.is_dir() else 'file'}, not a link")
        else:
            lines.append(f"{st:<10} {show(link, home)} -> {os.readlink(link)}")
    stale = [path for path, is_stale in unshipped_links(home, settings, links) if is_stale]
    for path in stale:
        lines.append(f"stale      {show(path, home)} -> {os.readlink(path)}; its target is gone")
    counts["stale"] += len(stale)
    if stale:
        lines.append(f"fix:       run ctlhq-install to remove the {len(stale)} stale link{'' if len(stale) == 1 else 's'}")
    if rules:
        st = rules_state(rules)
        counts[st] += 1
        shown = show(rules.path, home)
        if st == "link":
            lines.append(f"link       {shown} -> {os.readlink(rules.path)}; install replaces the link with the generated file")
        elif st == "copy":
            lines.append(f"copy       {shown} is a real {'folder' if rules.path.is_dir() else 'file'} without the generated-file marker")
        elif st == "stale":
            lines.append(f"stale      {shown} differs from the layers' home/AGENTS.md; install rewrites it")
        elif st == "managed":
            lines.append(f"managed    {shown} has a block managed by {managed_tools(rules)} that differs from the layers; "
                         "copy the new block into a layer's home/AGENTS.md")
        elif st == "missing":
            lines.append(f"missing    {shown}")
    if unwanted:
        counts["unwanted"] += 1
        lines.append(f"unwanted   {show(home / RULES, home)} is a generated file, but agents_md is not true; "
                     "install backs it up and removes it")
    for n, layer in enumerate(layers, 1):
        t = per_layer[layer]
        print(f"layer {n}    {layer}: {len(t['skills'])} skills, {t['agents']} agents, {t['links']} links, {t['ok']} ok")
    for line in lines:
        print(line)
    drift = sum(v for k, v in counts.items() if k != "ok")
    print(f"check: {summary(counts, kinds)}; {'clean' if drift == 0 else f'{drift} drift'} ({layer_count(settings)}, home {home})")
    return 1 if drift else 0


def install_rules(home: Path, rules: Rules, dry: bool, replace: bool, counts: dict) -> str:
    """ok, written, copy (left in place) or managed (kept)."""
    pre = "would " if dry else ""
    shown = show(rules.path, home)
    st = rules_state(rules)
    if st == "ok":
        counts["ok"] += 1
        if dry:
            print(f"ok           {shown}")
        return "ok"
    if st == "managed":
        print(f"managed      {shown}: its block managed by {managed_tools(rules)} differs from the layers; not overwritten. "
              "Copy the new block into a layer's home/AGENTS.md, then run install again")
        counts["managed kept"] += 1
        return "managed"
    if st == "copy":
        if not replace:
            print(f"copy         {shown}: copy in place, not replaced (--replace moves it to ~/.ctlhq-backups/)")
            counts["copies left"] += 1
            return "copy"
        back_up(home, rules.path, pre, dry)
        counts["backed up"] += 1
    if st == "link":
        print(f"{pre}remove link {shown} (was {os.readlink(rules.path)}); its target is not changed")
        if not dry:
            rules.path.unlink()
    print(f"{pre}write      {shown} from {len(rules.sources)} layer rules files")
    if not dry:
        write_rules(rules)
    counts["written"] += 1
    return "written"


def do_install(home: Path, settings: Settings, links: list, rules: Optional[Rules], dry: bool, replace: bool,
               save_setting: bool) -> int:
    pre = "would " if dry else ""
    layers = settings.layers
    keys = ("ok", "linked", "repointed", "backed up", "copies left", "extra removed", "stale removed")
    unwanted = unwanted_rules(home, rules)
    keys += ("written", "managed kept") if rules else ("rules removed",) if unwanted else ()
    counts = {k: 0 for k in keys}
    for link, source, wanted, _layer in links:
        if not wanted:
            if link.is_symlink() and inside_layers(link_target(link), layers):
                print(f"{pre}remove extra {show(link, home)} (host not listed for this skill)")
                if not dry:
                    link.unlink()
                counts["extra removed"] += 1
            continue
        st = state(link, source, layers)
        if st == "ok":
            counts["ok"] += 1
            if dry:
                print(f"ok           {show(link, home)}")
            continue
        if st == "copy":
            if not replace:
                print(f"copy         {show(link, home)}: copy in place, not replaced (--replace moves it to ~/.ctlhq-backups/)")
                counts["copies left"] += 1
                continue
            back_up(home, link, pre, dry)
            counts["backed up"] += 1
        elif st != "missing":
            print(f"{pre}repoint    {show(link, home)} (was {os.readlink(link)})")
            if not dry:
                link.unlink()
            counts["repointed"] += 1
        else:
            counts["linked"] += 1
        print(f"{pre}link       {show(link, home)} -> {source}")
        if not dry:
            link.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
            os.symlink(str(source), str(link))
    for path, is_stale in unshipped_links(home, settings, links):
        if is_stale:
            print(f"{pre}remove stale {show(path, home)} (was {os.readlink(path)}; its target is gone)")
            if not dry:
                path.unlink()
            counts["stale removed"] += 1
    if rules:
        st = install_rules(home, rules, dry, replace, counts)
        if save_setting:
            setting = show(home / SETTINGS, home)
            if st in ("ok", "written"):
                if not dry:
                    save_agents_md(home)
                print(f"{'would set' if dry else 'set'}        agents_md = true in {setting}")
            elif st == "copy":
                print(f"not set      agents_md = true in {setting}: {show(rules.path, home)} is your own file. "
                      "To use the generated file, run again with --agents-md --replace (your file moves to "
                      "~/.ctlhq-backups/). To keep your file, do nothing; later runs leave it alone.")
            else:
                print(f"not set      agents_md = true in {setting}: copy the new block into a layer's home/AGENTS.md, "
                      "then run --agents-md again")
    elif unwanted:
        back_up(home, home / RULES, pre, dry)
        print(f"{pre}remove     {show(home / RULES, home)} (generated file, agents_md is not true; backed up)")
        counts["backed up"] += 1
        counts["rules removed"] += 1
        print_include_note()
    print()
    print("Apply these yourself (the installer does not edit shell files or settings.json):")
    print(f'  PATH line, for ~/.zshrc:   export PATH="{ROOT}/bin:$PATH"')
    hook = {"type": "command", "command": f"{ROOT}/bin/ctlhq-reply-lint --hook", "timeout": 5}
    print('  Stop hook, the "Stop" key inside "hooks" in ~/.claude/settings.json '
          '(if "Stop" exists, add the inner {"type": ...} object to its "hooks" list):')
    print(f'    "Stop": {json.dumps([{"hooks": [hook]}])}')
    print()
    print(f"{'dry run' if dry else 'install'}: {summary(counts, keys)} ({layer_count(settings)}, home {home})")
    return 1 if counts["copies left"] or counts.get("managed kept") else 0


def do_uninstall(home: Path, settings: Settings, links: list, dry: bool) -> int:
    pre = "would " if dry else ""
    removed = kept = left = 0
    rules_path = home / RULES
    rules_gone = False
    for path in [link.path for link in links] + [rules_path]:
        if not path.is_symlink():
            continue
        if inside_layers(link_target(path), settings.layers):
            print(f"{pre}remove     {show(path, home)}")
            if not dry:
                path.unlink()
            removed += 1
            rules_gone = rules_gone or path == rules_path
        else:
            print(f"keep       {show(path, home)} -> {os.readlink(path)} (outside every layer)")
            kept += 1
    if is_generated(rules_path):
        back_up(home, rules_path, pre, dry)
        print(f"{pre}remove     {show(rules_path, home)} (generated file, backed up)")
        removed += 1
        rules_gone = True
    for path, is_stale in unshipped_links(home, settings, links):
        if is_stale:
            print(f"{pre}remove     {show(path, home)} (its target is gone)")
            if not dry:
                path.unlink()
            removed += 1
        else:
            print(f"left       {show(path, home)} -> {os.readlink(path)} (a name no layer ships; delete it yourself)")
            left += 1
    if rules_gone:
        print_include_note()
    if settings.agents_md:
        print(f"agents_md = true stays in {show(home / SETTINGS, home)}. Delete that line, "
              "or a later install writes ~/.codex/AGENTS.md again.")
    print(f"{'dry run' if dry else 'uninstall'}: {removed} removed, {kept} kept, {left} left for you to delete "
          f"({layer_count(settings)}, home {home})")
    return 0


def main(argv: list) -> int:
    flags = {"--dry-run": False, "--check": False, "--uninstall": False, "--replace": False, "--agents-md": False}
    home = None
    i = 0
    while i < len(argv):
        a = argv[i]
        if a in ("-h", "--help"):
            print(__doc__.strip())
            return 0
        if a in flags:
            flags[a] = True
        elif a == "--home":
            if i + 1 >= len(argv):
                return usage_error("--home needs a folder")
            home = argv[i + 1]
            i += 1
        elif a.startswith("--home="):
            home = a.split("=", 1)[1]
        else:
            return usage_error(f"unknown argument: {a}")
        i += 1
    if flags["--check"] and (flags["--uninstall"] or flags["--dry-run"] or flags["--replace"] or flags["--agents-md"]):
        return usage_error("--check takes only --home")
    if flags["--uninstall"] and (flags["--replace"] or flags["--agents-md"]):
        return usage_error("--uninstall does not combine with --replace or --agents-md")
    home_path = Path(home if home is not None else os.path.expanduser("~")).expanduser()
    if not home_path.is_dir():
        return usage_error(f"home folder not found: {home_path}")
    home_path = Path(os.path.realpath(home_path))
    dry = flags["--dry-run"]
    try:
        settings = load_settings(home_path)
        save_setting = flags["--agents-md"] and not settings.agents_md
        if save_setting:
            if (home_path / SETTINGS).is_symlink():
                raise ValueError(f"{home_path / SETTINGS} is a link; replace it with a real file, then run --agents-md again")
            settings = settings._replace(agents_md=True)
        links, rules = build_plan(home_path, settings)
        if flags["--check"]:
            return do_check(home_path, settings, links, rules)
        if flags["--uninstall"]:
            return do_uninstall(home_path, settings, links, dry)
        return do_install(home_path, settings, links, rules, dry, flags["--replace"], save_setting)
    except Duplicates as e:
        print(str(e))
        print("ctlhq-install: the same name in two layers is refused; nothing changed. Remove one copy.")
        return 1
    except ValueError as e:
        return usage_error(str(e))


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
